<title>USA: U.S. weekly soybean crush 30,732,000 bushels.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekly soybean crush 30,732,000 bushels.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Oilseed Processors Association weekly soybean crushings by reporting members (crushings/capacity in bu, soymeal exports in short tons):</p>
<p>			 12/11/96    12/04/96	Year-Ago</p>
<p> Crushings	 30,732,000  30,213,000    27,397,000</p>
<p> Capacity-X	34,948,000  34,948,000    33,569,000</p>
<p> Capacity-Y	35,140,728  35,140,728	     N/A</p>
<p> Meal Exports	 174,759     162,396	     N/A</p>
<p>X-Members reporting weekly. Y-Weekly reporters plus members reporting only monthly. N/A-Not Available. Totals may agree due to rounding by NOPA. R-revised.  </p>
<p>NOPA reported the following soybean crushings and capacity use by state for the week, with comparisons, in bushels:</p>
<p>    CRUSHINGS --   12/11/96    12/04/96     Year-Ago</p>
<p> Illinois	   5,504,000   5,416,000     4,933,000</p>
<p> Ind, Ky, Ohio    5,195,000   5,195,000     4,304,000</p>
<p> Southeast	  5,137,000   4,983,000     4,737,000</p>
<p> South Central    3,143,000   2,629,000     2,670,000</p>
<p> Southwest	  4,277,000   4,230,000     3,699,000</p>
<p> Iowa		 5,514,000   5,482,000     5,158,000</p>
<p> Minn,ND,SD,Mont  1,962,000   2,277,000     1,896,000</p>
<p> Total U.S.	30,732,000  30,213,000    27,397,000</p>
